  "keyedAbout": "The hardware-key screens (#355: Journey, Type It, QRQ Speed), whose decoder the screen cannot clear, hand each decoded run to 'keyed' and the key input's end-of-keying pause to 'paused'; the machine keeps the run keyed since the miss. Read by the same three readers as 'cases'.",
  "keyedDerivation": "Worked from the design rule, not by running any port. Same states, 'miss' and 'reset' as above; both also empty the kept run. 'keyed' while idle -> inactive. While awaiting: atMs - missAtMs < debounceMs -> debounced, and the chunk is dropped, not kept (the inclusive boundary as above). Otherwise the chunk is appended to the kept run, with its leading spaces dropped when the run is empty or ends in a space; if the run, trimmed, is at least as long as the target it is judged as 'input' would judge it (advance or wrong) and the kept run is emptied; otherwise 'pending' (nothing judged, still awaiting). 'paused' while idle -> inactive. While awaiting: the kept run, trimmed, is taken and the kept run emptied; empty -> pending; else judged as 'input' would judge it at that atMs. 'expect': pending means the call returns no outcome.",
